      "content": "These intermittent glitching errors often point to electromagnetic interference (EMI) from the ship's power grid or internal sensor errors leaving the temperature readings uncorrected. You should physically verify if internal wiring is touching other components or if the control board is overheating due to poor ventilation even inside the sealed unit. Transmitting a snapshot of your error logs to the manufacturer's support team immediately will likely provide the specific diagnostic needed to identify the defective component.",
